# This is not a production command: -R0 creates a changing endpoint.
# In the Pinggy dashboard, reserve and validate a persistent TLS passthrough
# mapping to 127.0.0.1:8443. Then put its foreground command in the private
# release file as PINGGY_TCP_COMMAND. It must preserve TLS/SNI and HTTP/2.
# Verify Pinggy's SSH host-key fingerprint through a trusted Pinggy channel,
# then add the verified gateway key to portals-svc's known_hosts. Remove any
# generated `StrictHostKeyChecking=no`. Final command must include
# `-o StrictHostKeyChecking=yes` and
# `-o UserKnownHostsFile=/Users/portals-svc/.ssh/known_hosts`.
